BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  # The Tale of the First Bridge) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite sides of a great chasm. The people of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    East Village possessed seeds but no water. The people of West Village had a flowing spring b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ut barren soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  One day, a young woman from the East approached the edge. She took a handful of her precious s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    eeds and cast them into the void, trusting the wind. The seeds, carried by ancient magic, mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ltiplied threefold as they crossed the chasm, landing in West Village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The people of the West marveled at this gift. They planted the seeds beside their spring, and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    soon had abundant crops. In gratitude, they filled their largest vessel with water and sent ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    it back across the chasm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  Seeing this reciprocity, the woman sent more seeds. The West sent more water. With each exchan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ge, trust grew like roots intertwining beneath the earth. The magic of the chasm blessed the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ir cooperation, and soon both villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  Eventually, the villagers built a bridge across the chasm - not from stone or wood, but from t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    he invisible threads of mutual trust they had woven.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
