BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite sides of a great chasm. The people) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (         of East Village possessed seeds but no water. The people of West Village had a flowing ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        spring but barren soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      One day, a young woman from the East approached the edge. She took a handful of her precio) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        us seeds and cast them into the void, trusting the wind. The seeds, carried by ancient m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        agic, multiplied threefold as they crossed the chasm, landing in West Village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      The people of the West marveled at this gift. They planted the seeds beside their spring, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        and soon had abundant crops. In gratitude, they filled their largest vessel with water a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        nd sent it back across the chasm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      Seeing this reciprocity, the woman sent more seeds. The West sent more water. With each ex) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        change, trust grew like roots intertwining beneath the earth. The magic of the chasm ble) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ssed their cooperation, and soon both villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      Eventually, the villagers built a bridge across the chasm - not from stone or wood, but fr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        om the invisible threads of mutual trust they had woven.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      The elders teach: *What you cast into the void with trust returns threefold, but only if t) Tj ET
